# AI Rules

> Hard, non-negotiable constraints for code generation in this project.
> **Update Trigger:** Modify when language version, tooling, or conventions change.

## Language & Runtime

- **Language:** [Python 3.12+ / TypeScript 5.x / etc.]
- **Package Manager:** [uv / npm / pnpm / etc.]
- **Runtime:** [CPython / Node.js / Deno / etc.]

## Code Organization

- [All new modules must have a module-level docstring]
- [Functions use keyword-only arguments after `*` separator]
- [No single-method service classes — use plain functions]

## Function Signatures

- [All public functions must have type annotations]
- [Use `*` separator for keyword-only arguments]
- [Return types are always explicit]

## Formatting & Linting

- **Formatter:** [ruff format / prettier / etc.]
- **Linter:** [ruff / eslint / etc.]
- **Line length:** [100 / 80 / etc.]
- **Run before commit:** `[linting command]`

## Type Checking

- **Tool:** [mypy / pyright / tsc / etc.]
- **Strictness:** [strict / basic / etc.]
- **Run:** `[type check command]`

## Testing

- **Framework:** [pytest / vitest / jest / etc.]
- **Run:** `[test command]`
- **Coverage minimum:** [80% / 90% / etc.]

## Docstrings

- **Format:** NumPy-style (see `.context/testing.md` for full standard)
- **Required sections:** Summary, Parameters, Returns
- **STRICT mode sections:** Position, Invariants, Raises, Silences
